00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.560
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.560
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.930
<i>いっさいがっさい Yes! SONIC!!</i>

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.930
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.930
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.910
<i>アブナイヨと Have A Nice は似てる</i>

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.910
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.910
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>そう　どちらも紙一重なのさ</i>

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:18.890
<i>タイクツ脱ぎ捨てて　今すぐかけだせ</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:18.890
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:18.890
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:22.390
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:22.390
<i>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</i>

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.640
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.640
<i>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</i>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.560
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.560
<i>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</i>

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.360
We know that Chris used this device to go to Sonic's world.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.160
Father, do you know anything else?

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:45.660
Chris locked the device so that no one else can teleport after him.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.330
That means we can't go?

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.420
No...

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.460
However...

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.630
According to my analysis, we can still send objects.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.100
That means...

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:07.870
Episode 59

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:07.870
Chaotix, Go Into Space

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.150
I wonder how Cream and her friends doing...

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.990
I hope they're okay.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.330
This belongs to Chris-

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.140
Charmy, answer the phone!

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:47.730
Ouch!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.100
What are you doing?

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.770
If you don't answer soon, they're going to hang up.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:51.810
Sheesh!

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.360
This is the Chaotix Detective Agency.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.780
Cream's mother!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.860
Thank you for your help last time.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:03.370
It was no biggie.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.330
I want to hire you again.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.700
All right, I'll be right over!

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:09.960
Ouch!

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.580
What's so funny!

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.260
Don't cry.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:22.260
Okay.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.390
Where's Espio?

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:25.350
Over there.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.890
Charmy, bring the black pepper!

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:31.560
Okay.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.560
Grind grind grind...

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.780
I am not a steak!

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:45.490
Cream went into space with Sonic and his friends.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.870
Can you check up on her in my place?

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:53.710
And while you're at it, it would be great if you can deliver these to Chris.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.460
All these boxes to Sonic's spaceship.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.710
Okay, Cream's mom! Piece of cake!

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:00.760
Vector!

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.180
What is it, Espio?

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.010
It won't be a piece of cake.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.180
Why not?

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.930
We don't have a spaceship, so how are we going into outer space?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.730
You have a point.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.570
Now it's a piece of cake.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.450
I'm counting on you.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.540
All clear ahead!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.790
All clear ahead!

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.380
When there are no Metarex, outer space is peaceful.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.760
Yes, very peaceful.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.510
Hurry up!

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:54.060
I'm going for a run while Knuckles makes up his mind.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.940
This will be a great move!

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:03.990
How's that!

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.990
Sonic, where did you go?

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.370
Sonic!

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:11.540
Hey!

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.910
It's your turn!

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.130
Sonic!

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:29.470
This is bad! Even Sonic can't come back if he has nothing to run on!

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:32.970
A rope? What do you need with a rope?

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:35.390
Sonic went flying off into outer space!

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.520
Fine! I'll go and rescue him!

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.770
You don't know where he is!

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.070
The longer we wait, the further away he gets!

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:49.200
Follow me! We can't let anything happen to Sonic!

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.540
Sonic, I'll be right there!

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:07.590
What's going on?

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:09.300
Look at that!

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.100
Is that a spaceship?

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.970
Tails! Chris!

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.430
We have no data on that ship.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:16.930
Is it Metarex?

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:20.730
It doesn't have any weapons.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.690
Where are Sonic and Knuckles?

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:28.320
Sonic flew into outer space, so Knuckles went to rescue him.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.990
If you told us, we could've rescued him with the Blue Typhoon!

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:36.080
We have to fight on our own until they return.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:40.290
Will we be able to beat them?

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:42.040
We can't afford to lose!

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.470
We caught up sooner than we thought.

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.550
This is delicious!

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.300
Stop acting like a pig!

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.850
When we arrive, I'll be the first to greet them.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.320
Outer space is cold.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.490
I guess that's the way.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.950
Everyone, let's do it as we planned.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.410
Hey!

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:19.960
It opened.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:27.840
What happened?

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:31.760
I was ambushed. I don't know what's going on.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.430
Vector, pull yourself together!

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.010
In that case, I'll check it out.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:49.150
Geez, who scraped off the paint during the commotion?

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:54.320
Glare!

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:57.540
Amy?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:58.700
What's wrong?

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.080
That!

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.000
It's an invisible Metarex!

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.210
Let's beat it up!

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:11.050
I was beaten up.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.720
They also painted you.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:15.550
How embarrassing! It's my biggest blunder ever!

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:17.850
I'll have to start my training from scratch.

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:20.100
It's my turn to go!

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.140
Charmy.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:22.310
What is it, Vector?

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:26.230
Wear full armor so that you'll be ready for anything.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.110
Okay!

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.110
Everyone, it's teatime!

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:31.780
We have cake.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:35.410
You have good timing! I was just getting thirsty.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.450
It looks delicious! Who made it?

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:42.210
Mama taught me how to make this cake.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:44.790
Wow! Teach me how to make it next time!

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.540
Same here.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:48.500
Hello!

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.340
Metarex?

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.510
Beat it up!

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:54.300
Yeah!

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:55.470
What?

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.450
They've become super violent since the last time we met them!

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:20.710
They won't get away with this! We only came because Cream's mother asked us to deliver her packages!

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:25.590
Our intentions are good! They're so rude!

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:26.210
Ouch...

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.840
Let's just go home.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.470
You idiot! What are you talking about?

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:35.010
Once we accept a job, we finish it, no matter what!

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:39.520
That's why a Chaotix detective is a man among men!

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:46.440
But we can't work because we're hurt.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:49.860
We should withdraw and think of a new strategy.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:54.320
What's wrong? We're leaving right now.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.240
It's delicious!

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.200
What's up, Chris?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.370
It looks like they're fleeing.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.580
What?

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.460
I'm going to finish them off!

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:09.840
Can you handle them by yourself, Tails?

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:13.380
He'll be fine. They seem really weak.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:14.680
Leave them to me!

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.050
Sure. You'll defeat them easily.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:23.140
Huh?

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:26.060
Somebody must be talking about me.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:28.690
It's hard being popular.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.940
It's more likely that they're making fun of you.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.540
Here I go, Metarex!

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:09.940
X-Tornado, taking off!

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.660
That house looks familiar.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:26.040
Can it be?

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:32.550
Just as I thought!

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:36.380
Hey, Vector! Espio! Charmy!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.470
He's calling us.

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:39.430
What should we do?

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.470
The best strategy is to retreat.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:44.560
They're planning to finish us off, Vector.

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:46.180
You're right.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:49.060
Let's lose them at full speed!

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:57.990
They left...

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:01.120
It's impossible to follow them in the X-Tornado.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.700
This is Chris.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:06.620
That spaceship is very fast.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:09.750
You're right, so I need to ask you for a favor.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.000
What is it?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:15.420
Can you chase that spaceship and capture it using the Blue Typhoon's hand?

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.130
No problem!

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:20.180
Blue Typhoon! Turn 180 degrees!

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:26.640
Pursue Metarex's spaceship!

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.020
Umm...

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:32.440
They weren't Metarex...

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.440
What is it, Charmy?

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.570
The bigger one is chasing us this time.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.450
What?

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:47.200
Damn! We'll lose them, even if it means using up all the fuel we have!

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:48.460
Stop it, Vector!

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:55.340
I told you so!

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:57.130
Cool!

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.260
It stopped.

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:01.220
We're saved.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:03.090
You're wrong...

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:08.810
We've captured the small spaceship and are bringing it into our ship.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:13.690
Tails, who's inside the ship?

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:16.480
It's not Metarex?

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:21.030
I'm sorry.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.410
We're sorry!

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:27.330
Since it's all cleared up, it's fine.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:28.500
It's fine!

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:30.710
Everyone makes mistakes.

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:32.920
Let bygones be bygones.

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:37.420
Help us unload Chris's packages off the ship.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.460
Here!

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:56.520
Grandpa made that spaceship.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.150
That's everything.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:04.200
Thank you, Vector. I'll clear the rest myself.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:05.320
Okay.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:12.250
Mom and Dad, thank you.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:16.130
This is how they show that they care about me.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:28.310
It's time to go home.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:30.140
Hey!

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:31.730
Vector! Espio! Charmy!

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:33.810
Have tea with us before you leave!

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.730
We also have cake.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:37.690
Yay! Cake!

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:40.400
No thanks. We did what we came here to do.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.070
Hold it, Espio.

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:46.660
It's fine. We must accept their goodwill.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.450
Would you like seconds?

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.500
I'll have some.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:54.330
Okay.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.040
By the way, Cream...

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.170
Yes?

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:02.510
I don't know if it's right for me to say, but are you sure this is okay?

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:04.970
To stay here and play around?

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.930
How rude! I'm not playing around!

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:14.680
That's right! As a Blue Typhoon crewman, Cream faces the dangers of space and carries out her duties!

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:18.310
But your mother is worried about you back home!

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.230
About what?

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:24.610
Cream needs to get married soon!

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.150
Or something like that.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:29.160
My mother doesn't think like that!

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:31.830
She will never force me to get married!

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.000
Cosmo, let's go!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:39.000
You made Cream angry.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.290
You should've kept your mouth shut.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:45.720
I thought that was an excellent impersonation of Cream's mother!

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:51.260
Hold on. Even though Cream's mother didn't specifically say so, maybe she wanted us to-

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:54.180
Stop, Vector! Don't assume anything!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:58.650
I'm sure that she wanted to say that Cream...

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:03.570
Vector, please bring Cream back!

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:08.660
As her mother, I can't bear to think that Cream is in trouble!

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:09.570
Mother!

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:12.330
Please understand how I feel!

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:16.200
I know you understand, Vector!

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.170
Of course I understand!

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.790
You don't understand at all!

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:26.460
It's started again! Vector's imagination is getting carried away, and no one can stop him!

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.680
I'm taking Cream home!

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:29.550
Why?

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:30.840
Because!

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:34.640
It's a promise I made with Cream's mother!

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:36.680
You never made such a promise!

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:40.690
Our hearts made that promise!

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:43.480
We made eye contact!

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:47.320
He's speaking complete nonsense!

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:51.160
I'm going to put Cream in this bag and take her home!

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.370
No one can stop him!

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.790
No one can stop crazy Vector!

00:16:56.950 --> 00:17:01.170
I don't think there any Chaos Emeralds in this space sector.

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:04.420
It's because the gravitational field is low.

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:06.340
The odds of finding one are slim.

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:07.800
How about this direction?

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:10.880
It's nearby, and the direction is also correct.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.720
Yes, I see.

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:15.810
Then let's narrow the search area a little more.

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:18.640
Well, we're leaving!

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:21.900
You should stay a bit longer.

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:24.520
I'll make the cake this time.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:26.730
No, we really don't want that.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.030
I'm gonna beat you up!

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:29.650
Anyway, we're leaving.

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:32.070
We have a lot of clients, so we have to hurry.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.200
Bye!

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.660
They left.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:40.040
Where are Cream and Cheese?

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:42.710
Come to think of it, Cosmo isn't around either.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:46.710
They were all here until Vector arrived.

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:50.510
What are you doing?

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.340
You're going home to your mother.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.220
Me too?

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.760
When did you get in there?

00:17:56.760 --> 00:18:00.810
I wasn't sure if I could trust you.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:07.860
You really were villains!

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:10.240
I was suspicious from the start!

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:11.320
Especially you!

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:14.110
This has nothing to do with you!

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.370
Hurry up and return to that ship!

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:21.790
No! I won't leave without Cream!

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:22.830
Wait!

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.790
No, I won't wait!

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:28.380
Cosmo, do your best!

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:29.170
I will!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:31.510
That looks like a lot of fun!

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:33.550
That looked painful.

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:35.010
What's the matter?

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:37.550
They're going to catch us!

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:43.440
I'll be successful this time.

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:52.610
One...two...three!

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:58.450
I failed.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.830
They sure try hard.

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:05.710
You shouldn't be admiring them! They kidnapped Cream!

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:08.630
Let's see if the hands can handle it!

00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:11.210
You flew pretty far.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:12.840
Thank you, Knuckles!

00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:16.840
I'll go on ahead!

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:18.390
You just leave?

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:21.520
Is it easy to fix?

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:22.520
Of course!

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:24.890
As long as Chris and I work together!

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.390
Let's do it!

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:28.860
Sonic!

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:30.480
We were worried about you!

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.860
Cream, Cheese and Cosmo...

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:36.860
Vector kidnapped them!

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:40.870
Damn! I can't speed up!

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:48.670
There it is.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.720
Sonic!

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:01.720
I'm taking Cream and my friends back!

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:07.770
I can't allow that. Cream's mother asked us to bring her home.

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:11.020
That's a lie! Mama would never ask you to do that!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:13.320
Espio and Charmy, is that true?

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.150
Well...

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:20.870
Trust me!

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:27.120
According to my instincts, Cream's mother, without saying a word, wanted me to bring her home.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:30.000
Instincts? Without saying a word?

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.500
Oops!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:35.170
But there's no denying that Cream's mother is worried about her!

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:37.420
You're trying to sever the bond between a mother and her child!

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.340
I won't let you do that!

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:41.720
Playtime's over!

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:46.310
I'm taking Cream back!

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:54.150
Please stop!

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:59.070
You're all trying to take Cream without asking how she feels!

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:01.320
You're all selfish!

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:07.790
Everyone, she's right.

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:12.710
Cream chose to come on this trip.

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:17.460
Whether Cream decides to continue or not is her decision.

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:20.970
I understand, but you know how parents are.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:23.430
I know. However...

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:31.350
A real family stays connected, no matter how far apart they are.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.480
What do you want to do, Cream?

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:36.980
I want to continue my journey.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:40.990
I left without telling her, but I'm sure Mama understands.

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:44.620
Espio, Charmy!

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:45.990
We're leaving!

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:48.580
Mission accomplished.

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:51.370
But I want to play longer!

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:58.090
Cream!

00:21:58.090 --> 00:21:58.760
Yes?

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:01.680
Make sure to contact your mother every now and then.

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:02.970
I will!

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:09.560
Huh?

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:22.700
Finally!

00:22:22.700 --> 00:22:24.110
I can't wait!

00:22:32.290 --> 00:22:34.040
No way...

00:22:34.710 --> 00:22:36.080
This is...

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:54.140
<i>私たちの世界は　魔法をかけられて</i>

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:54.140
<b>Watashitachi no sekai wa mahou o kakerarete</b>

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:54.140
<i><i>There’s magic cast on our world.</i></i>

